@startuml Notification-System-Use-Case
title Notification System - Use Case Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Mobile App User" as MobileUser
actor "System" as System
actor "Golang Service" as GolangService
actor "FCM Server" as FCM

rectangle "Notification System" {
  
  package "Mobile Client Operations" {
    usecase "Register FCM Token" as UC1
    usecase "Update FCM Token" as UC2
    usecase "Receive Push Notification" as UC3
    usecase "Handle Foreground Notification" as UC4
    usecase "Handle Background Notification" as UC5
    usecase "Handle Quit State Notification" as UC6
  }
  
  package "Backend Operations" {
    usecase "Store FCM Token" as UC7
    usecase "Validate Token" as UC8
    usecase "Publish Event to Kafka" as UC9
  }
  
  package "Notification Service (Golang)" {
    usecase "Consume Kafka Message" as UC10
    usecase "Process Notification Payload" as UC11
    usecase "Send FCM Notification" as UC12
    usecase "Store Notification History" as UC13
    usecase "Handle Send Failure" as UC14
  }
  
  package "Notification Management" {
    usecase "View Notification History" as UC15
    usecase "Mark as Read" as UC16
    usecase "Delete Notification" as UC17
  }
}

' Mobile User relationships
MobileUser --> UC1
MobileUser --> UC2
MobileUser --> UC3
MobileUser --> UC4
MobileUser --> UC5
MobileUser --> UC6
MobileUser --> UC15
MobileUser --> UC16
MobileUser --> UC17

' System relationships
System --> UC7
System --> UC8
System --> UC9

' Golang Service relationships
GolangService --> UC10
GolangService --> UC11
GolangService --> UC12
GolangService --> UC13
GolangService --> UC14

' Include relationships
UC1 .> UC7 : <<include>>
UC2 .> UC7 : <<include>>
UC7 .> UC8 : <<include>>

UC9 .> UC10 : <<include>>
UC10 .> UC11 : <<include>>
UC11 .> UC12 : <<include>>
UC12 .> UC13 : <<include>>

UC12 --> FCM
UC3 <-- FCM

' Extend relationships
UC12 ..> UC14 : <<extend>>

note right of UC9
  Task creation, updates, and
  other events are published
  to Kafka topic
end note

note bottom of UC10
  Golang notification service
  consumes from Kafka and
  sends FCM notifications
  via Firebase Admin SDK
end note

note left of UC13
  Notification history stored
  in PostgreSQL database for
  audit and retrieval
end note

note right of UC3
  React Native app receives
  notifications in different
  states (foreground, background, quit)
end note

@enduml
